==Old English==
===Alternative spellings===
'''ehta''', '''ahta'''

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/'æahta/}}

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|ahto|lang=ang}} from {{proto|Indo-European|oktō(u)-|eight|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old High German [[ahto]] (German [[acht]]), Old Saxon [[ahto]] (Dutch [[acht]]), Old Norse ''átta'' (Swedish [[åtta]]), Gothic [[𐌰𐌷𐍄𐌰𐌿]]; and, outside the Germanic languages, with Sanskrit {{term|अष्ट|tr=aṣṭa|lang=sa|sc=Deva}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ὀκτώ|tr=oktō|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Latin [[octo]], Albanian [[tetë]], Old Irish [[ocht]] (Irish [[hocht]]), Old Slavic ''osm’'' (Russian {{term|восемь|lang=ru|sc=Cyrl|tr=vósem’}}).

===Numeral===
